knext bundled fix for vinext 1.0.1 (dist output)
Upstream: https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/pull/3684
What it fixes: A request path with a repeated slash or a backslash (`//`, `/docs//`, `//evil.com`) gets Next.js's 308 to the collapsed path (query kept, Location always same-origin) instead of a 404 or a thrown URL parse. A bare `//` therefore redirects to `/` and serves the index route. Percent-encoded leading `%2F`/`%5C` and any collapsed path that is still open-redirect shaped keep their 404.
This is the maintainer's version of the PR (it replaced the earlier "bare // is not an open redirect"
change): new redirect helpers in open-redirect.js, wired into the App Router / Pages / SSR request
entries, the Node production server, and the dev server (after its origin check, before the
public/_next conflict guard).
Retire: delete this file (and its manifest entry) when the pinned vinext is >= the first
release that includes cloudflare/vinext#3684.
Ported by hand from the upstream src change to the published 1.0.1 dist files.
Applied by `knext vinext-patches` (runs from the app's postinstall and before `knext build`).

